<task id="090" project="spaarkeai-compose-r8">
  <metadata>
    <title>Wrap-up — anti-clobber deploy · /test-diet · write-side fidelity doc · lessons-learned · INDEX + root §17 update</title>
    <phase>8 Wrap-up</phase>
    <gate>blocked-on-all</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Project-close mechanics and documentation; implementation was reviewed in its owning tasks.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical with clear oracles: the deploy either pairs both artifacts, `/test-diet` emits its report, the INDEX row either matches reality or does not. The judgment in this project was spent in tasks 020–074.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Deploys shared environments and updates repo-wide indexes.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>017, 023, 031, 045, 053, 063, 070, 071, 072, 073, 074</deps>
    <tags>devops, documentation, deployment</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close the project properly.

    1. **Anti-clobber deploy** — BFF and `sprk_spaarkeai` together, same tree, one window (NFR-05). Never from
       a net8 tree.
    2. **`/test-diet`** — MANDATORY at project close (root CLAUDE.md §7). It reconciles tests added during R8
       against the ADR-038 §7 build-vs-maintain classifier and emits `git rm`/`git mv` commands for reviewer
       judgment. It is read-only — do NOT auto-execute its output. Report to
       `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/test-diet-report.md`; the wrap-up PR MUST cite it.
    3. **Write-side fidelity companion doc** — the counterpart to
       `docs/architecture/COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md`: the merge mechanism, the seven invariants, the
       residual loss list pointer, and the extension recipe for a future contributor.
    4. **Lessons-learned** — including the one the project turned on: seven releases of engine investment
       (Half A, "what bytes to write") while the client contract (Half B, "did it arrive and did we tell the
       truth") got none, and why the seam tests were structurally incapable of catching it.
    5. **Indexes** — `projects/INDEX.md` row updated; root CLAUDE.md §17 Compose pointer refreshed to name the
       write-side doc alongside the read-side one; god-class ratchet row updated for the deleted waivers.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE DevOps + documentation engineer. Familiar with the anti-clobber deploy pair, `/test-diet`, and the repo's documentation pointers.</role>

  <goal>
    R8 is deployed as a matched pair, its tests are reconciled against ADR-038, the write-side architecture is
    documented, lessons are recorded, and every index that names Compose is current.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Root CLAUDE.md §7 makes `/test-diet` a HARD WARNING if skipped at project close, and the wrap-up PR must
      cite the report or document the skip rationale. Root §17's Compose row currently points only at the
      read/reference fidelity doc — R8 is the write side, and leaving §17 unchanged would send the next
      contributor to the wrong document.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="doc-output">docs/architecture/ (write-side fidelity companion)</file>
      <file role="doc-output">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/lessons-learned.md</file>
      <file role="doc-output">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/test-diet-report.md</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">projects/INDEX.md</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">CLAUDE.md (§17 Compose pointer)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/patterns/testing/god-class-ratchet.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-05">Deploy BFF and `sprk_spaarkeai` TOGETHER, same tree, one window. Never from a net8 tree.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §7">`/test-diet` is MANDATORY at project close. It is READ-ONLY — do NOT auto-execute its `git rm`/`git mv` output. The wrap-up PR MUST cite the report.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3">Root `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/` edits are MAIN SESSION only — sub-agents cannot write those paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §18">Any PR touching root CLAUDE.md MUST add an entry to `.claude/CHANGELOG.md`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">The write-side doc COMPLEMENTS `COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md`. MUST NOT duplicate its content.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The god-class ratchet row in root §17 MUST reflect the ACTUAL number of remaining Compose waivers after Track D — if task 074 recorded NOT-CONFIRMED, say five-minus-four, not five-minus-five.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`/conflict-check` before the PR. Report final publish size (absolute + delta vs 44.96 MB).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>project close, deployment pairing, documentation pointers</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/guides/ENVIRONMENT-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/god-class-ratchet.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor declaration">Declare rigor STANDARD; load spec.md + CLAUDE.md.</step>
    <step order="1">Run `/conflict-check`. Confirm the TFM is net10.</step>
    <step order="2">Deploy BFF + `sprk_spaarkeai` together from the same tree.</step>
    <step order="3">Run `/test-diet`; write the report; do NOT execute its output.</step>
    <step order="4">Write the write-side fidelity companion doc in `docs/architecture/`.</step>
    <step order="5">Write lessons-learned, including the Half-A/Half-B finding and why the seam tests could not catch Half B.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `projects/INDEX.md`; update root CLAUDE.md §17 (Compose pointer + god-class ratchet row) with the ACTUAL waiver count; add the `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry.</step>
    <step order="7">Open the wrap-up PR citing the test-diet report and the final publish size.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any Track's gate did not pass (Track S UAT, the Phase-3 gate, the fidelity gate in CI), do NOT close the project. Report what is outstanding — a wrap-up over an unmet gate is how the next release inherits the same defect.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">docs/architecture/ (write-side fidelity companion)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/lessons-learned.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/test-diet-report.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/INDEX.md</output>
    <output type="doc">CLAUDE.md</output>
    <output type="doc">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>BFF and `sprk_spaarkeai` were deployed together from the same net10 tree, in one window.</criterion>
    <criterion>`/test-diet` was run, its report written, and the wrap-up PR cites it.</criterion>
    <criterion>The write-side fidelity companion doc exists in `docs/architecture/` covering the merge mechanism, the seven invariants, the residual-list pointer, and an extension recipe.</criterion>
    <criterion>Lessons-learned records the Half-A/Half-B finding and why the seam tests were structurally incapable of catching Half B.</criterion>
    <criterion>`projects/INDEX.md` is updated; root CLAUDE.md §17 names the write-side doc and states the ACTUAL remaining Compose waiver count.</criterion>
    <criterion>`.claude/CHANGELOG.md` has an entry for the root CLAUDE.md change.</criterion>
    <criterion>`/conflict-check` was run; final publish size reported (absolute + delta vs 44.96 MB).</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: `/test-diet` output was NOT auto-executed.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: the write-side doc does not duplicate `COMPOSE-READ-REFERENCE-FIDELITY.md`.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: the project was not closed over an unmet gate.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
